.\" GriddyWM man page
.TH GRIDDY 1 "2026-05-23" "GriddyWM 0.1" "GriddyWM Manual"

.SH NAME
griddy \- Grid-based Wayland compositor

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B griddy
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-check\fR]
[\fB\-\-replace\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-xwayland\fR]
[\fB\-\-backend\fR \fIwinit|drm\fR]
[\fB\-\-gpu\fR \fIdevice\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B griddy
is a Wayland compositor built around a 2-D NxN grid of workspaces.
Each workspace has six tiled slot positions (two halves and four quarters)
plus unlimited floating, fullscreen, and total-fullscreen window states.
Windows stack within slots and the user navigates spatially in all four
cardinal directions (and diagonally) across the grid.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIpath\fR
Override the config file location.
Defaults to the first of:
.IR $GRIDDY_CONFIG ,
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/griddy/config.toml ,
.IR ~/.config/griddy/config.toml ,
.IR /etc/griddy/config.toml .

.TP
.B \-\-check
Parse all config files (config.toml, theme.toml, rules.toml,
workspace-templates.toml, plugins.toml), print any errors, then exit.
Exit code 0 = valid, 1 = error.
Does not start the compositor.
Useful in CI / dotfiles automation.

.TP
.B \-\-replace
Send SIGTERM to the currently running
.B griddy
instance (identified by the PID file in
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/griddy.lock ),
wait up to 3 seconds for it to exit (SIGKILL if it doesn't), then start
this instance.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-xwayland
Disable XWayland for this session regardless of config.

.TP
.BR \-\-backend " " \fIwinit|drm\fR
Select the rendering backend.
.B winit
(default) runs inside an existing Wayland or X11 session — useful for
development and testing.
.B drm
drives a real TTY via KMS/DRM (production; not yet implemented).

.TP
.BR \-\-gpu " " \fIdevice\fR
Pin the render GPU, e.g.
.IR /dev/dri/card1 .
No-op in the winit backend.

.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable debug logging (equivalent to
.IR RUST_LOG=griddy=debug ).

.SH CONFIGURATION
The compositor loads config files from the config directory in this order:

.TP
.B config.toml
Main configuration: grid dimensions, input, windows, keybinds, submaps,
overview, animations, OSD, startup commands, and environment variables.
A commented default is copied to
.I ~/.config/griddy/config.toml
on first launch.

.TP
.B theme.toml
Visual configuration: colors, gaps, borders, cursor, blur.
Auto-loaded from the same directory as
.BR config.toml .

.TP
.B rules.toml
Per-application window rules: match by
.B app_id
or
.B title
glob; set slot, state, workspace, floating geometry, opacity, pin.

.TP
.B keybinds.toml
Extra keybind entries appended to the main table.

.TP
.B workspace-templates.toml
Workspace templates (§8.10): define per-workspace application layouts
applied on first visit.

.TP
.B plugins.toml
Out-of-tree plugin list (§13): each
.B [[plugin]]
entry specifies a path to a shared library implementing the GriddyWM
plugin ABI.

.SH IPC
The compositor exposes two UNIX sockets in
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/griddy/griddy_<PID>/ :

.TP
.B .command.sock
Request/response.
Prefix commands with
.B j/
to receive JSON output.

.TP
.B .events.sock
Push-only event stream (one event per line:
.IR eventname>>data ).

See
.BR griddyctl (1)
for the full command and event catalogue.

.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown.

.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Force config reload (same as
.BR "griddyctl reload" ).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GRIDDY_CONFIG
Override config file path.

.TP
.B GRIDDY_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE
Set by the compositor to
.IR griddy_<PID>
and inherited by all child processes.

.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Set by the compositor to the socket name
.RI ( griddy-N ).

.TP
.B XDG_SESSION_TYPE
Set to
.BR wayland .

.TP
.B XCURSOR_THEME ", " XCURSOR_SIZE
Set from
.IR theme.toml " [cursor]"
on startup and on reload.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/griddy/config.toml
Per-user main configuration (created from default on first launch).

.TP
.I /usr/share/griddy/default.toml
Commented default configuration (source for first-run copy).

.TP
.I /usr/share/wayland-sessions/griddy.desktop
Session file for display managers (LightDM, SDDM, GDM, greetd).

.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/griddy.lock
PID file (used by
.BR \-\-replace ).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR griddyctl (1),
.BR wayland (7)

